   "id": "temurah.12b.5",
   "daf": "12b",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "וְאֵין מֵי חַטָּאת (נַעֲשֶׂה) [נַעֲשִׂין] מֵי חַטָּאת כּוּ׳. מַאן תַּנָּא? אָמַר רַבִּי חִיָּיא בַּר אַבָּא אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: דְּלָא כְּרַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And the water of purification» of the red heifer «becomes water of purification only» with the placement of the ashes into the water, but not by the placement of water onto the ashes. The Gemara asks: «Who is the tanna» whose opinion is reflected in this ruling? «Rabbi Ḥiyya bar Abba said» that «Rabbi Yoḥanan said that» it is «not in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Shimon.»"
  }
